id: pm-gh1710
title: "GH-1710: budget compaction clips next_cursor to 240 characters, so --after rejects the cursor the page emitted and the rest of the result set is unreachable"
description: "GH-1710 (filed 2026-11-12). When pm list compacts its output to fit an output budget, it shortens next_cursor like any other long string: the cursor is cut to 240 characters plus an ellipsis while the page still says has_more true, so --after rejects it with invalid_query_cursor and the rest of the result set is unreachable. Reproduced on main 145286488: eight items with 180-character ids and 2,000-character titles, pm list --json --output-budget 2000 --limit 4 (with or without --for triage) emits a 241-character cursor ending in an ellipsis instead of the 351-character one. Root cause: both string-compaction walkers, compactStrings in src/sdk/read-output-budget.ts and compactContextIntentValue in src/sdk/context-intent-contracts.ts, shorten every string longer than 240 characters, and the producer cursor is rebased only when rows are dropped, so a string-only compaction keeps the clipped value. Fix: a continuation token (key cursor or ending in _cursor) is never shortened in either walker, and a cursor argument carrying an ellipsis is refused with invalid_query_cursor reason cursor_compacted (read_output_cursor_invalid for --output-cursor) naming the larger-budget read that returns it whole."
type: Issue
status: in_progress
priority: 1
tags[5]: agent-ux,"gh:1710",output-budget,pagination,read-output
